Objective: Visit in order — 1) nearest rock, 2) nearest container, 3) nearest car. At least 3.0 m from any object centroid for nav goals. Confirm each stop before proceeding.

Loop per target class:
1) At each stopped pose, lidar will perform both get_lidar_snapshot and get_semantic_lidar_objects. Camera will capture an image and optional histogram.
2) If semantic lidar returns a centroid for the current target class, planner computes a nav goal offset ≥3.0 m from the centroid toward spawn (0,0): goal = centroid + 3.0*(spawn-centroid)/||spawn-centroid||. Navigator will navigate_to_pose to that goal.
3) After navigator reports success (reached within ~2.5 m), lidar will call confirm_stop(<class>). If lidar confirm_stop true → mark visited and proceed to next class. If lidar confirm_stop false or lidar cannot confirm, camera will call confirm_stop(<class>) as fallback.
4) If lidar does not report the target centroid at a stop, navigator will move to the next exploration viewpoint from the sequence: (3,0), (0,3), (-3,0), (0,-3), repeating as needed. get_occupancy_map will only be requested after a nav failure or if planner needs alternate free-cell viewpoints.
5) If navigator fails to reach a planned goal twice, call get_occupancy_map and pick a different free cell viewpoint away from already-seen objects, then navigate there and sense again.

Roles summary:
- navigator: execute navigation goals; never sense or confirm.
- lidar: at every stop take get_lidar_snapshot AND get_semantic_lidar_objects; use semantic centroids for planning; after navigator success, call confirm_stop(<class>) as primary confirmer.
- camera: capture image/histogram at stops; call confirm_stop(<class>) only if lidar cannot confirm.

After all three ordered stops are confirmed, planner will call report_mission_done with the visited classes in order.

